Notebook[{
Cell["\<\
Five-point seed: wide-angle Landshoff versus central-soft MRK\
\>", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"ab905d78-edc3-4d6d-8a9c-16f5b6187df1"],

Cell["\<\
This notebook compares the F polynomial for the same two-loop six-propagator \
graph and the same external attachment order {1,2,3,5,4}. It separates the \
exact coplanar wide-angle on-shell expansion from the central-soft MRK \
composite expansion. Every region vector is displayed in the convention \
(v_x0,...,v_x5;1).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"16c386b8-513b-4a8b-aebf-b88ac810340a"],

Cell["1. Reproducible setup", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"fc1db057-b864-4692-bc4e-2968c3186411"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"$HRF5ComparisonLibraryOnly", "=", "True"}], ";", 
  RowBox[{"Get", "[", 
   RowBox[{"FileNameJoin", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"NotebookDirectory", "[", "]"}], 
      ",", "\"\<HRF_FivePointWideAngleCentralSoftComparison.wl\>\""}], "}"}], 
    "]"}], "]"}], ";", 
  RowBox[{"comparison", "=", 
   RowBox[{"hrf5WideAngleCentralSoftComparison", "[", "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",\
ExpressionUUID->"e61958ab-d2e2-4d70-8bf8-043d8304e615"],

Cell["\<\
The graph has internal edges x0:(1,3), x1:(1,5), x2:(2,3), x3:(2,5), \
x4:(3,4), x5:(4,5). External momenta are attached to vertices in the order \
{1,2,3,5,4}; this is the representative attachment that has the central-soft \
MRK hidden region.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8109946d-84f3-474b-9054-ed1c2bce5374"],

Cell["2. Common exact transverse chart", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"9d5e20d2-0bf7-44f0-8866-079dce934c83"],

Cell["\<\
Use p3_perp=q, p4_perp=k and p5_perp=-q-k, with w=-p3_perp/p4_perp and \
wbar=-conjugate(p3_perp)/conjugate(p4_perp). The exact wide-angle coplanar \
branch has finite nonzero q and k with w=wbar=-q/k. The central-soft MRK \
limit instead sends k to zero, so w and wbar become large.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9aa303fe-6ca4-493e-aecd-aa37eb5a4f69"],

Cell["2.1 Exact light-cone coefficients used below", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"547e717f-c660-4cc3-a74a-d4198b363050"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[GridBox[{
    {
     StyleBox["\<\"symbol\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     StyleBox["\<\"definition\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     StyleBox["\<\"meaning\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold]},
    {"\<\"P\"\>", "\<\"p3+ = P delta^(-b)\"\>", "\<\"upper-jet longitudinal \
normalization\"\>"},
    {"\<\"K\"\>", "\<\"p4+ = K delta^a\"\>", "\<\"central-emission \
longitudinal normalization\"\>"},
    {"\<\"M\"\>", "\<\"p5- = M delta^(-b)\"\>", "\<\"lower-jet longitudinal \
normalization\"\>"},
    {"\<\"T\"\>", "\<\"|p3_perp|^2 = T\"\>", "\<\"fixed upper transverse \
scale\"\>"},
    {"\<\"R\"\>", "\<\"|p4_perp|^2 = R delta^(2a)\"\>", "\<\"rescaled central \
transverse scale\"\>"},
    {"\<\"C\"\>", "\<\"2 Re(p3_perp conjugate(k_perp)) = C\"\>", \
"\<\"transverse interference; C^2 <= 4 T R\"\>"}
   },
   AutoDelete->False,
   GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}},
   GridBoxBackground->{"Columns" -> {{None}}, "Rows" -> {
       RGBColor[0.94, 0.96, 0.99], None}},
   GridBoxFrame->{"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}},
   GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{1.}}, "Rows" -> {{0.65}}}],
  "Grid"]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"83e38dd1-3daa-4b8e-8b5e-2fb87d1ca73d"],

Cell["\<\
All P,K,M,R,T are positive. The sign of C records the relative transverse \
orientation; in a general physical configuration it obeys the transverse \
Cauchy-Schwarz bound.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0a98f503-8e26-43dc-b4a7-0ef662aedfee"],

Cell["2.2 Relation to the variables of the NNLL 2-to-3 MRK paper", \
"Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"76111bba-50ff-488b-95eb-72abc7633d61"],

Cell["\<\
The paper fixes {s,s1,s2,t1,t2}, or equivalently {s,s1,s2,z,zbar}, and varies \
the auxiliary parameter x. The central-soft limit is a composite path rather \
than ordinary MRK at fixed s1,s2,z,zbar:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8b7bd9af-5dc5-4a1d-8cde-09026fdb9bf7"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[GridBox[{
    {
     StyleBox["\<\"paper variable\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     StyleBox["\<\"invariants\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     StyleBox["\<\"central-soft scaling\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold]},
    {"\<\"x\"\>", "\<\"s12=s/x^2\"\>", "\<\"x=delta^b\"\>"},
    {"\<\"s\"\>", "\<\"hard energy coefficient\"\>", "\<\"s=P M\"\>"},
    {"\<\"s1\"\>", "\<\"s45=s1/x\"\>", "\<\"s1=K M delta^a\"\>"},
    {"\<\"s2\"\>", "\<\"s34=s2/x\"\>", "\<\"s2=(P R/K) delta^a\"\>"},
    {"\<\"t1\"\>", "\<\"t1=s15\"\>", "\<\"t1=-T-C delta^a-R \
delta^(2a)+...\"\>"},
    {"\<\"t2\"\>", "\<\"t2=s23\"\>", "\<\"t2=-T+...\"\>"},
    {"\<\"z,zbar\"\>", "\<\"t1=-(1-z)(1-zbar)s1 s2/s; t2=-z zbar s1 \
s2/s\"\>", "\<\"z=Z delta^(-a), zbar=Zbar delta^(-a)\"\>"}
   },
   AutoDelete->False,
   GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}},
   GridBoxBackground->{"Columns" -> {{None}}, "Rows" -> {
       RGBColor[0.94, 0.96, 0.99], None}},
   GridBoxFrame->{"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}},
   GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{1.}}, "Rows" -> {{0.65}}}],
  "Grid"]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"b0d8727c-ed8f-4fef-a097-f04b68497130"],

Cell["\<\
The finite rescaled variables satisfy Z Zbar=T/R and Z+Zbar=-C/R. The exact \
transverse variables used later in that paper are w=-p3_perp/p4_perp, \
wbar=-conjugate(p3_perp)/conjugate(p4_perp), X34=p3+/p4+, and X45=p4+/p5+, \
together with one dimensionful transverse scale. Along the central-soft path, \
w~delta^(-a), X34~delta^(-(a+b)), and X45~delta^(a-b).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d2698b0b-aa7e-45d4-b452-6530d7f56435"],

Cell["3. Coplanar wide-angle on-shell expansion", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"b4fb7860-0024-44b7-9677-0ec524406043"],

Cell["\<\
Here p_i^2=lambda tends to zero while all adjacent invariants remain \
wide-angle and the massless endpoint satisfies Gram=0. The polynomial is \
F=F0+lambda F1. With all x_e scaling as lambda^(-1), F0 has raw weight -3, \
whereas U and lambda F1 have weight -2.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ae0a2d9b-f684-4101-b5a8-8392e0792b28"],

Cell["3.1 Positive Landau locus and local coordinates", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"dc03ab81-178d-4f2a-a2fe-3d38439b9076"],

Cell["\<\
The following replacement rules define three normal coordinates y0,y2,y4 \
around the positive Landau locus. The remaining x1,x3,x5 are internal \
coordinates along it.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2277c9c3-b57b-422f-93d1-801dd01627ad"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"x0", "\[Rule]", 
      RowBox[{
       FractionBox[
        RowBox[{"aPlus", " ", "kTrans", " ", "x1", " ", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"bPlus", " ", "mMinus"}], "+", 
           SuperscriptBox["kTrans", "2"], "+", 
           RowBox[{"kTrans", " ", "qTrans"}]}], ")"}]}], 
        RowBox[{"bPlus", " ", "qTrans", " ", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"aPlus", " ", "mMinus"}], "+", 
           RowBox[{"kTrans", " ", "qTrans"}], "+", 
           SuperscriptBox["qTrans", "2"]}], ")"}]}]], "+", "y0"}]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"x2", "\[Rule]", 
      RowBox[{
       FractionBox[
        RowBox[{"x3", " ", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"bPlus", " ", "mMinus"}], "+", 
           SuperscriptBox["kTrans", "2"], "+", 
           RowBox[{"kTrans", " ", "qTrans"}]}], ")"}]}], 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"aPlus", " ", "mMinus"}], "+", 
         RowBox[{"kTrans", " ", "qTrans"}], "+", 
         SuperscriptBox["qTrans", "2"]}]], "+", "y2"}]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"x4", "\[Rule]", 
      RowBox[{
       FractionBox[
        RowBox[{"kTrans", " ", "x5"}], "qTrans"], "+", "y4"}]}]}], "}"}],
   TraditionalForm],
  TraditionalForm,
  Editable->True]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"0ae5989d-023e-4d03-ba10-\
5f29401381f2"],

Cell["3.2 Exact factorised superleading sector", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"fde74a1c-a334-408b-a5f4-3f70b83a9124"],

Cell["\<\
In these coordinates the constant and linear terms vanish identically. There \
is also no cubic normal-coordinate term. The complete F_SL=F0 is the \
quadratic form\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5466371a-ac34-49ca-b053-84c4294c0310"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"-", 
     FractionBox[
      RowBox[{"x1", " ", "y2", " ", "y4", " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"aPlus", " ", "bPlus", " ", "mMinus"}], "+", 
         RowBox[{"aPlus", " ", 
          SuperscriptBox["kTrans", "2"]}], "+", 
         RowBox[{"bPlus", " ", 
          SuperscriptBox["qTrans", "2"]}]}], ")"}]}], "bPlus"]}], "-", 
    RowBox[{
     FractionBox["1", 
      RowBox[{"aPlus", " ", "mMinus"}]], 
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox["qTrans", "2"], " ", "x3", " ", "y0", " ", "y4", " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"aPlus", " ", "mMinus"}], "+", 
        RowBox[{"bPlus", " ", "mMinus"}], "+", 
        SuperscriptBox["kTrans", "2"], "+", 
        RowBox[{"2", " ", "kTrans", " ", "qTrans"}], "+", 
        SuperscriptBox["qTrans", "2"]}], ")"}]}]}], "+", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"x5", " ", "y0", " ", "y2", " ", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"aPlus", " ", "mMinus"}], "+", 
         RowBox[{"kTrans", " ", "qTrans"}], "+", 
         SuperscriptBox["qTrans", "2"]}], ")"}], "2"]}], 
     RowBox[{"aPlus", " ", "mMinus"}]]}],
   TraditionalForm],
  TraditionalForm,
  Editable->True]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"8aabe617-1d78-40c6-8e69-\
8d36a415a113"],

Cell["\<\
where all three coefficient functions below are positive for positive \
light-cone data:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1807c6fe-0fea-4373-822e-1878cf3e4651"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[GridBox[{
    {
     StyleBox["\<\"coefficient\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     StyleBox["\<\"value\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold]},
    {"AWA", 
     FractionBox[
      SuperscriptBox[
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"aPlus", " ", "mMinus"}], "+", 
         RowBox[{"kTrans", " ", "qTrans"}], "+", 
         SuperscriptBox["qTrans", "2"]}], ")"}], "2"], 
      RowBox[{"aPlus", " ", "mMinus"}]]},
    {"BWA", 
     FractionBox[
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox["qTrans", "2"], " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         SuperscriptBox["kTrans", "2"], "+", 
         RowBox[{"aPlus", " ", "mMinus"}], "+", 
         RowBox[{"bPlus", " ", "mMinus"}], "+", 
         RowBox[{"2", " ", "kTrans", " ", "qTrans"}], "+", 
         SuperscriptBox["qTrans", "2"]}], ")"}]}], 
      RowBox[{"aPlus", " ", "mMinus"}]]},
    {"CWA", 
     FractionBox[
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"aPlus", " ", 
        SuperscriptBox["kTrans", "2"]}], "+", 
       RowBox[{"aPlus", " ", "bPlus", " ", "mMinus"}], "+", 
       RowBox[{"bPlus", " ", 
        SuperscriptBox["qTrans", "2"]}]}], "bPlus"]}
   },
   AutoDelete->False,
   GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}},
   GridBoxBackground->{"Columns" -> {{None}}, "Rows" -> {
       RGBColor[0.94, 0.96, 0.99], None}},
   GridBoxFrame->{"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}},
   GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{1.}}, "Rows" -> {{0.65}}}],
  "Grid"]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"0092ce23-1d62-46a6-84c9-8e935c657b87"],

Cell["3.3 Scaling", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"73bdf32c-f961-4528-89df-0bd74de6ba82"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[GridBox[{
    {
     StyleBox["\<\"object\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     StyleBox["\<\"weight\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold]},
    {"\<\"original LP parameters (x0,...,x5)\"\>", "\<\"(-1,-1,-1,-1,-1,-1;1)\
\"\>"},
    {"\<\"internal coordinates (x1,x3,x5)\"\>", "\<\"(-1,-1,-1)\"\>"},
    {"\<\"symmetric normal coordinates (y0,y2,y4)\"\>", "\<\"(-1/2,-1/2,-1/2)\
\"\>"},
    {"\<\"raw F_SL\"\>", "\<\"W_SL=-3\"\>"},
    {"\<\"F_SL after cancellation; U; lambda F1\"\>", "\<\"W_HR=-2\"\>"}
   },
   AutoDelete->False,
   GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}},
   GridBoxBackground->{"Columns" -> {{None}}, "Rows" -> {
       RGBColor[0.94, 0.96, 0.99], None}},
   GridBoxFrame->{"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}},
   GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{1.}}, "Rows" -> {{0.65}}}],
  "Grid"]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"ae9d52cd-b6ba-48df-8dd7-d773bcc3cae1"],

Cell["\<\
The symmetric local presentation has y0,y2,y4 proportional to lambda^(-1/2). \
Each term x_i y_j y_k in F_SL therefore has weight -2, exactly matching U and \
lambda F1. The original-variable HR vector remains the uniform vector; the \
half-integer weights refer only to the dissected local normal coordinates.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cb7964cf-105f-4e0b-a365-d39316c7c327"],

Cell["4. Central-soft MRK expansion", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"10b588ac-f14f-4f54-b23d-05b89bde55bc"],

Cell["\<\
For the representative path p4_perp~delta and x_MRK~delta^2, asymptotic-order \
alignment produces the first vector below. The later vectors were previously \
reported as an HRF composition, but the next-layer audit below shows that \
they must be rejected.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e8e80724-9ae9-4842-abf3-ac496001a69c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[GridBox[{
    {
     StyleBox["\<\"stage\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     StyleBox["\<\"vector (x0,...,x5;1)\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold]},
    {"\<\"asymptotic-order alignment\"\>", "\<\"(-3,-3,0,-3,-3,-3;1)\"\>"},
    {"\<\"would-be HRF scaling in the aligned variables\"\>", \
"\<\"(-1,-1,-1,-1,-1,-1;1)\"\>"},
    {"\<\"rejected composed scaling in the original variables\"\>", \
"\<\"(-4,-4,-1,-4,-4,-4;1)\"\>"},
    {"\<\"raw superleading F layer\"\>", "\<\"W=-13\"\>"},
    {"\<\"first obstruction\"\>", "\<\"W=-12\"\>"}
   },
   AutoDelete->False,
   GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}},
   GridBoxBackground->{"Columns" -> {{None}}, "Rows" -> {
       RGBColor[0.94, 0.96, 0.99], None}},
   GridBoxFrame->{"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}},
   GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{1.}}, "Rows" -> {{0.65}}}],
  "Grid"]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"12b8f904-8144-403c-859b-559082a0fee8"],

Cell["4.1 The aligned leading factorisation", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"b591130f-2c89-4689-9610-74612c19c160"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"-", "M"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"P", " ", "x2"}], "-", 
      RowBox[{"K", " ", "x3"}]}], ")"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"x1", " ", "x4"}], "-", 
      RowBox[{"x0", " ", "x5"}]}], ")"}]}],
   TraditionalForm],
  TraditionalForm,
  Editable->True]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"86964f28-a654-4a7c-a878-\
a473ff52e662"],

Cell["\<\
At the leading aligned level the candidate locus is simultaneous: P x2-K x3=0 \
and x1 x4-x0 x5=0. It is not a union of coordinate boundaries. This leading \
statement alone is insufficient because the next aligned layer must also be \
examined.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c76243fe-afaf-4bda-8e94-327392ea79b2"],

Cell["4.2 The full sequence of F layers", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"f5b83546-d062-4e76-9b4b-0a60c93c0525"],

Cell["\<\
After applying the would-be composed vector, the layers beginning at the raw \
superleading weight -13 are:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"68c1fb00-5674-423f-88b4-feaec5f23c43"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[GridBox[{
    {
     StyleBox["\<\"delta weight\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     StyleBox["\<\"coefficient polynomial\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold]},
    {
     RowBox[{"-", "13"}], 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "M"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"P", " ", "x2"}], "-", 
        RowBox[{"K", " ", "x3"}]}], ")"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"x1", " ", "x4"}], "-", 
        RowBox[{"x0", " ", "x5"}]}], ")"}]}]},
    {
     RowBox[{"-", "12"}], 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", "T"}], " ", "x0", " ", "x3", " ", "x4"}]},
    {
     RowBox[{"-", "11"}], 
     RowBox[{"C", " ", "x1", " ", "x3", " ", "x4"}]},
    {
     RowBox[{"-", "10"}], 
     FractionBox[
      RowBox[{"R", " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "P"}], " ", "x1", " ", "x2", " ", "x4"}], "+", 
         RowBox[{"2", " ", "K", " ", "x1", " ", "x3", " ", "x4"}], "-", 
         RowBox[{"P", " ", "x1", " ", "x2", " ", "x5"}], "-", 
         RowBox[{"K", " ", "x0", " ", "x3", " ", "x5"}]}], ")"}]}], "K"]},
    {
     RowBox[{"-", "9"}], 
     RowBox[{"-", 
      FractionBox[
       RowBox[{"T", " ", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"K", " ", "M", " ", "P", " ", "x1", " ", "x2", " ", "x4"}], 
          "+", 
          RowBox[{
           SuperscriptBox["K", "2"], " ", "M", " ", "x0", " ", "x3", " ", 
           "x4"}], "-", 
          RowBox[{"P", " ", "R", " ", "x1", " ", "x3", " ", "x4"}], "-", 
          RowBox[{
          "2", " ", "K", " ", "M", " ", "P", " ", "x0", " ", "x2", " ", 
           "x5"}], "+", 
          RowBox[{
           SuperscriptBox["K", "2"], " ", "M", " ", "x0", " ", "x3", " ", 
           "x5"}]}], ")"}]}], 
       RowBox[{"K", " ", "M", " ", "P"}]]}]},
    {
     RowBox[{"-", "8"}], 
     FractionBox[
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", "K"}], " ", 
        SuperscriptBox["T", "2"], " ", "x0", " ", "x3", " ", "x4"}], "+", 
       RowBox[{"C", " ", "P", " ", "R", " ", "x1", " ", "x3", " ", "x4"}], "+", 
       RowBox[{
       "C", " ", "K", " ", "M", " ", "P", " ", "x0", " ", "x2", " ", "x5"}]}], 
      RowBox[{"K", " ", "M", " ", "P"}]]}
   },
   AutoDelete->False,
   GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}},
   GridBoxBackground->{"Columns" -> {{None}}, "Rows" -> {
       RGBColor[0.94, 0.96, 0.99], None}},
   GridBoxFrame->{"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}},
   GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{1.}}, "Rows" -> {{0.65}}}],
  "Grid"]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"b923b9d1-048d-4a9a-838f-dbde09452dfc"],

Cell["\<\
The delta^(-12) coefficient is -T x0 x3 x4. It does not vanish on the \
two-factor locus and is strictly nonzero for T,x0,x3,x4>0. It is therefore a \
genuine obstruction, not a harmless deformation that may be skipped.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1f417c87-7f20-4517-b376-f7610e7d7279"],

Cell["4.3 Positive-stationarity test after alignment", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"adbb9a5a-0036-4521-9bb0-d0d7e93455ca"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"-", 
     RowBox[{"M", " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"P", " ", "x2"}], "-", 
        RowBox[{"K", " ", "x3"}]}], ")"}], " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"x1", " ", "x4"}], "-", 
        RowBox[{"x0", " ", "x5"}]}], ")"}]}]}], "-", 
    RowBox[{"T", " ", "x0", " ", "x3", " ", "x4"}]}],
   TraditionalForm],
  TraditionalForm,
  Editable->True]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"0ff3cf48-2647-468b-b41d-\
d57f42644b7b"],

Cell["\<\
The derivatives with respect to x1 and x2 force P x2-K x3=0 and x1 x4-x0 \
x5=0. After imposing these, the x0 derivative reduces to -T x3 x4, which \
cannot vanish in the positive interior. Hence the combined first two aligned \
layers have no positive stationary pinch. The previously reported vector \
(-4,-4,-1,-4,-4,-4;1) is rejected.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a4b84aaa-3846-4a6f-963b-9bea39aea3d9"],

Cell["5. Structural comparison", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"fb0cb380-fecf-4bf5-9165-f5c70eccd9c1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[GridBox[{
    {
     StyleBox["\<\"feature\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     StyleBox["\<\"wide-angle on-shell\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     StyleBox["\<\"central-soft MRK\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold]},
    {"\<\"kinematic route to Gram zero\"\>", "\<\"finite transverse momenta, \
w=wbar\"\>", "\<\"p4_perp -> 0; w,wbar -> infinity\"\>"},
    {"\<\"leading cancellation structure\"\>", "\<\"quadratic form in three \
linear normal coordinates\"\>", "\<\"leading product, immediately obstructed \
at the next layer\"\>"},
    {"\<\"LP-parameter vector\"\>", "\<\"uniform (-1,-1,-1,-1,-1,-1;1)\"\>", \
"\<\"previous nonuniform candidate is rejected\"\>"},
    {"\<\"cancellation hierarchy\"\>", "\<\"one gap: -3 -> -2\"\>", "\<\"-13 \
leading product; nonzero obstruction at -12\"\>"}
   },
   AutoDelete->False,
   GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}},
   GridBoxBackground->{"Columns" -> {{None}}, "Rows" -> {
       RGBColor[0.94, 0.96, 0.99], None}},
   GridBoxFrame->{"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}},
   GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{1.}}, "Rows" -> {{0.65}}}],
  "Grid"]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"e8d95a79-bb1d-4e0c-8eef-1785aa61d58b"],

Cell["\<\
The coplanar wide-angle on-shell region remains an exact positive Landau \
region. By contrast, the previously reported central-soft MRK candidate fails \
at the first obstruction after asymptotic-order alignment. Before drawing a \
wide-angle-to-MRK correspondence at five points, the remaining attachment \
orders and possible alternative scalings must be re-audited with this \
obstruction test enforced.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"751b354c-b069-44a6-8ccb-c6c5721afebc"]
},
WindowTitle->"Five-point wide-angle and central-soft F comparison",
FrontEndVersion->"15.0 for Mac OS X ARM (64-bit) (July 2, 2026)",
StyleDefinitions->"Default.nb",
ExpressionUUID->"4fa4d273-4bc6-416c-af3e-a4f66d6369e9"
]
